Origin: request to build an asdf skill for devs, companies, AI agents, and CI/CD,
after reading the asdf repo README, source, and docs/.

Research method
- Four parallel agents over docs/{guide,manage,plugins,more} plus the Go source.
- Every command and flag cross-checked against internal/cli/cli.go and a live
  asdf 0.18.0 binary. Docs alone were not trusted.

Source-of-truth findings that shaped the content
- asdf-vm/actions v4.0.0 is the first release supporting asdf 0.16+; v3 and
  earlier drive the 0.15 bash implementation only.
- use_release_candidates is commented out in the 0.16+ config struct and has no
  effect, despite still appearing in the official docs.
- Caching all of ~/.asdf breaks asdf-vm/actions (asdf-vm/actions#445); cache
  installs/, plugins/, downloads/ instead.
- Multi-tool plugin repos (asdf-community/asdf-hashicorp serves terraform,
  vault, consul, packer, nomad) select their tool by reading the basename of the
  directory asdf cloned them into, so the local plugin name is load-bearing.
- Plugin miss error, verified: "error fetching plugin URL: plugin <name> not
  found in repository".
- asdf list exits 0 even when its version filter matches nothing, and the filter
  is a prefix match, so exit-status checks for an installed version are wrong.

Validation
- Two eval iterations, 4 then 5 scenarios, each run with and without the skill
  and graded against per-scenario assertions.
- Iteration 1: 100% with skill vs 76% baseline. Gap concentrated in
  troubleshooting (6/6 vs 3/6) and CI (6/6 vs 4/6); onboarding tied at 6/6,
  i.e. the common path is already well covered by base knowledge.
- Baseline was advantaged: runs executed inside the asdf repo, and one baseline
  agent read cli.go to derive that asdf local was removed. The delta is
  therefore conservative.
- Iteration 2 added a plugin-sourcing scenario after review feedback that not
  every plugin resolves via a bare short name. With skill 8/8, baseline 7/8 —
  the baseline pinned asdf v0.14.1 and sourced asdf.sh in a script intended for
  every teammate and CI.

Post-eval static review (Codex) caught five defects the simulated runs missed,
all since fixed:
- GitHub Actions env: PATH: expands to "/.asdf/shims:" because the env context
  does not inherit the runner HOME/PATH, replacing rather than extending PATH.
- An installed-version check relying on asdf list exit status (see above).
- configure --prefix pointing at a temp dir, which bakes a deleted path into
  built artifacts; replaced with real prefix plus DESTDIR staging.
- Docker runtime stage copying ASDF_DATA_DIR without the asdf binary the shims
  invoke.
- PowerShell reading bare $ASDF_DATA_DIR (a script variable) instead of
  $env:ASDF_DATA_DIR; this bug is inherited verbatim from the upstream docs.

Known gap
- Nothing in the skill has been executed end to end. All evals were simulated
  and all verification was against source, the local binary, or static review.
  A sandbox smoke test of the onboarding flow and the generated plugin is the
  recommended next step.
